WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.940
Every file in the final image should have a reason to be there.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:11.000
The runtime image is not a backup of the repository and not a general troubleshooting workstation.

3
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:16.780
It should contain what the ASP.NET Core application needs to run and operate responsibly.

4
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:34.020
Runtime images should avoid unnecessary shells, package managers, compilers, curl or wget-style tools, source code, test data, sample files, package caches, and debugging utilities unless there is a documented production need.

5
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:38.760
Removing unneeded tools reduces image contents and simplifies review.

6
00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.200
Native dependencies need the same care as application dependencies.

7
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:54.420
Image packages, operating system libraries, graphics libraries, compression libraries, database drivers, and other native components should be tracked, scanned, patched, and removed when they are no longer needed.

8
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.500
Some operating system content is still necessary.

9
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:06.800
Certificates, CA bundles, timezone data, ICU and globalization support, font libraries, and native libraries may be required depending on the application.

10
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:15.060
Removing too aggressively can break authentication, date handling, localization, document generation, or outbound calls.

11
00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:26.620
Debug symbols, dumps, generated documentation, OpenAPI artifacts, diagnostics endpoints, and development-only configuration should be reviewed before shipping.

12
00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:36.240
These items may be useful in controlled workflows, but they can also expose implementation details or increase operational exposure when carried into production images.

13
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:40.920
Temporary data and build artifacts should not become permanent runtime content.

14
00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:46.300
The final image should reflect a release decision, not the accumulation of intermediate build products.

15
00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:50.980
Reducing contents reduces attack surface when compatibility is preserved.

16
00:01:51.080 --> 00:02:00.280
The balance is to ship only required runtime contents while retaining the operational observability and support paths the production service genuinely needs.
